DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     FreeBSD provides machine-independent bus support and raw drivers for
     ffiirreewwiirree interfaces.

     The ffiirreewwiirree driver consists of two layers: the controller and the bus
     layer.  The controller attaches to a physical bus (like pci(4)).  The
     ffiirreewwiirree bus attaches to the controller.  Additional drivers can be at‐
     tached to the bus.

     Up to 63 devices, including the host itself, can be attached to a
     ffiirreewwiirree bus.  The root node is dynamically assigned with a PHY device
     function.  Also, the other ffiirreewwiirree bus specific parameters, e.g., node
     ID, cycle master, isochronous resource manager and bus manager, are dy‐
     namically assigned, after bus reset is initiated.  On the ffiirreewwiirree bus,
     every device is identified by an EUI 64 address.

